{
  "id": "acute-tolerance",
  "term": "acute tolerance",
  "definition": "Acute tolerance is a rapid, within-session reduction in a drug’s intoxicating effect as the nervous system adjusts while the drug is still present. With alcohol, it means impairment is greater early in a drinking episode than later at a similar blood alcohol level, reflecting adaptation rather than faster metabolism.",
